# Update stage progress at the end of work

Ship through pull requests into `beta` (since 2 Nov 2026). `beta` is for testing. `main` is only stable code: a pull request from `beta` into `main` publishes the next release. Do not open feature pull requests against `main`. Keep CI runs few: one branch and PR per logical change, open it as a draft while iterating (drafts skip CI), push only after `pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm test` (and `pnpm e2e` for app changes) pass locally, and mark it ready once. CI is Linux only; add `ci:all-os` only for platform-specific changes, once, right before merge. Merges do not rerun CI (weekly `main` run plus manual dispatch). Docs and `.cursor/**` changes skip CI. Do not tag releases or run `package.yml` by hand. Full rules: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#shipping).

A task is not finished until the phase docs match what you just did. Do this in the **same commit** as the work. Do not leave it for a follow-up commit. This applies to features, fixes, docs, CI, and verification — not only new stages.

The human-readable copy of this rule lives in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md#end-of-work-update-progress).

## Files that must stay in sync

1. [docs/BUILD_STAGES.md](../../docs/BUILD_STAGES.md)
   - The **Progress** snapshot sentence and table (Status + Notes for every stage you touched).
   - That stage's **Checklist**: tick finished items; leave unverified items unchecked.
   - **Gotchas**: append anything you discovered the hard way.
   - **Appendix B** when you ran a manual agent matrix.
2. [docs/PLAN.md](../../docs/PLAN.md)
   - **Current phase**: **Now / Next / Blockers** in a short paragraph. Must match the Progress table.

## Status values

- `Not started`
- `In progress (PR #N)` while the PR is open, `In progress (PR #N, merged)` after merge without `arch-ok`
- `Blocked (reason)`
- `Done` or `Done (PR #N)` — only after the stage checklist and Omarchy/Hyprland `arch-ok`. Never from CI alone. Work from the direct-to-main period (30 Oct to 1 Nov 2026) names its commit on `main`.

## Notes column

Write what is true now: the PR and whether it is merged, CI result (name red jobs and link the run), what is left, what the next stage is. Do not leave "then merge" after the merge. When you finish a stage's code, mark the next unstarted stage's Notes as "Next stage" and name any hand-off that is already in place.

## Before you mark the PR ready

If `docs/BUILD_STAGES.md` and `docs/PLAN.md` are unchanged, the progress update is missing. Go back and write it.
